# Aston Martin DB2 fixed-head coupe, 1950-1953.
#
# The DB2, on sale from May 1950 to April 1953. The fixed-head coupe is the
# body modelled, not the drophead.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DB2 (The Motor road test, 1950,
# cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.128 x 1.651 x 1.359 m, wheelbase 2.515 m. Source: The Motor's
# 1950 road test, as given in the English Wikipedia infobox and recorded in the
# reference pack. The model's hull measures 4.119 m (8.4 mm short of the
# published figure) on the 2.515 m wheelbase (60.9 per cent), 1.651 m wide and
# 1.359 m high.
#
# Shape reference: three photographs of the 1950 car, registration 986 GV.
# The rounded post-war GT shape is modelled: long low bonnet, tall narrow
# grille, fastback roofline, partly enclosed rear wheels, wire wheels and the
# small round tail lamps low on the rear panel.
#
# Colours: no British-market colour list was found (grade d), and in this era
# cars were finished to order, so the objects carry plain names: British Racing
# Green, silver, black and red. Weights green 3, silver 3, black 2, red 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase. Chrome and the wire wheels
# keep their own materials.
#
# Speed 180 km/h, the car's quoted maximum. Comfort 55/413, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 55: a low, firm-riding GT of 1950 with little luggage space.
# Class 4.
#
# Dates are road presence: May 1950 intro, retires staggered 1963-1966 on a
# thirteen- to sixteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-db2.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-db2.dae (60 objects). References:
# citycars/references/aston-db2/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the photographed front wings are more distinct and the
# rear window larger and more rounded than the model's; the windscreen and one
# quarterlight stand 7.7-14.5 mm and 13.1-20.7 mm clear of the cabin, just
# outside the 10-20 mm rule at the low end. At 128 px the long bonnet, the tall
# grille and the fastback tail read as a DB2.

obj=citycar
name=AstonDB2(BritishRacingGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1950
intro_month=5
retire_year=1966
retire_month=6
speed=180
class=4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=55
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=413

Image[E]=./images/aston-db2-britishracinggreen_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/aston-db2-britishracinggreen_SE.0.0,-13,0
Image[S]=./images/aston-db2-britishracinggreen_S.0.0,0,0
Image[SW]=./images/aston-db2-britishracinggreen_SW.0.0,-8,10
Image[W]=./images/aston-db2-britishracinggreen_W.0.0,4,5
Image[NW]=./images/aston-db2-britishracinggreen_NW.0.0,12,10
Image[N]=./images/aston-db2-britishracinggreen_N.0.0,0,33
